# Standalone upstream-runtime reproducer; NOT a passing application test.
# Run with the pinned kc3s, no RTS bridge or project modules required.
# Numerically equal typed subjects can duplicate a fact in the hash table
# while the sorted index treats them as equal. Removing both can report
# "facts_remove_fact_local: skiplist_remove index_spo" (or assert in debug).
# Runtime sources are intentionally untouched. Do not use mixed-width aliases
# of the same subject/object in game data; geometry produces reduced integers.
require Facts
db = Facts.database()
Facts.add_tags(db, (S64) 0, :body, {1, 128, 128, 128})
Facts.add_tags(db, (Uw) 0, :body, {1, 128, 128, 128})
Facts.remove_tags(db, (S64) 0, :body, {1, 128, 128, 128})
Facts.remove_tags(db, (Uw) 0, :body, {1, 128, 128, 128})
puts("Reproducer completed; inspect stderr as well as exit status.")
